    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="0740" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.42/47</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1537</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-08">April 8,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received May 16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Legation’s despatches during the course of 1939 regarding the new education law
                    which the Iraqi Government was proposing to enact. After lying dormant for some
                    time, the proposal was revived a few days ago. It was brought to my attention
                    that a committee of the Chamber of Deputies which had the proposal under
                    consideration had finally prepared its report for presentation to the Chamber
                    and that this report recommended the law as previously drafted with certain
                    amendments which made it even more unacceptable so far as foreign schools were
                    concerned and which did not eliminate any of its former undesirable features. I
                    enclose a copy<anchor n="23" xml:id="d669-f1"/> of what is believed to be the
                    text of the previous law with the committee’s recommendations in parallel
                    columns.</p>
                <pb facs="0741" n="729" xml:id="pg729"/>
                <p>Immediately the matter came to my attention I consulted with my French and
                    British colleagues and I afterwards addressed a first-person note to the Acting
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs, a copy of which I enclose. The French Minister is
                    making strong representations in the matter, and the British Ambassador,
                    although there are no British schools in Iraq, intends to support the
                    representations of the French Minister and myself.</p>
                <p>I will keep the Department informed of developments.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d669-a1.xml" xpointer="d669-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
